2. In these Regulations, unless the context otherwise requires —
“approved responsible gambling programme” means a responsible gambling programme approved by the Authority under regulation 5(4)(a) for a casino, and includes such programme as amended from time to time with the approval of the Authority under regulation 7, 9 or 11;
“approved review report” means a review report approved by the Authority under regulation 8(6)(a);
“problem gambling” means any gambling addiction or pathological gambling behaviour;
“Responsible Gambling Code for Casinos” means the code issued by the Authority under section 200B of the Act which relates to responsible gambling and includes such code as amended by the Authority from time to time in accordance with that section;
“responsible gambling measure” means any practice or activity by the casino operator of a casino during its operation which is designed —
(a)to reduce the severity of harm to patrons, vulnerable persons and society at large caused by casino gambling; or
[S 652/2026 wef 21/09/2026]
(b)to help in the making of informed decisions about casino gambling;
[S 652/2026 wef 21/09/2026]
“responsible gambling programme”, in relation to the casino operator of a casino or applicant for a casino licence, means a programme which contains details of the establishment, operation and implementation of responsible gambling measures carried out or proposed to be carried out by the casino operator (or applicant) for the casino during its operation;
[S 652/2026 wef 21/09/2026]
“review” means the review referred to in regulation 8(1);
“review report” means the report of the review referred to in regulation 8(3).

5.—(1) An applicant for a casino licence must submit to the Authority for approval a responsible gambling programme for the applicant’s proposed casino at the same time as the applicant submits its application for a casino licence or within such period after the application as the Authority may allow in any particular case.
[S 652/2026 wef 21/09/2026]
(2) A responsible gambling programme submitted to the Authority for approval under paragraph (1) must contain all of the following information in respect of the casino to which the application relates:
(a)the goals, targets, performance indicators of the responsible gambling programme and timelines to meet all responsible gambling requirements in the Responsible Gambling Code for Casinos;
(b)the person or committee appointed or to be appointed by the casino operator to supervise the establishment, operation and implementation of the responsible gambling programme if approved, and details of the duties and responsibilities of such person or committee;
[S 652/2026 wef 21/09/2026]
(c)procedures and guidelines to identify any patron of the casino with any suspected or known problem gambling or gambling-related problem;
[S 652/2026 wef 21/09/2026]
(d)procedures and guidelines with respect to the availability of information, treatment, counselling services or intervention services to any patron of the casino regarding problem gambling, responsible gambling behaviour and the financial, social and other problems that may arise in connection with gambling behaviour;
[S 652/2026 wef 21/09/2026]
(e)details of the establishment, operation and implementation by the casino operator of a system to enable a patron of the casino to set limits on the patron’s casino gambling expenditure or period of continuous casino gambling;
[S 652/2026 wef 21/09/2026]
(f)details of the establishment, operation and implementation by the casino operator of a system to exclude specific patrons;
(g)details of the establishment, operation and implementation by the casino operator of a system to determine and impose a maximum number of visits which a patron may make to the casino in each month;
[S 652/2026 wef 21/09/2026]
(h)details of a training programme for casino employees of the casino operator in promoting or adopting responsible measures in the conduct of casino gambling, including details of the training curricula and plans for periodic refresher training;
[S 652/2026 wef 21/09/2026]
(i)procedures and guidelines for the keeping of records related to responsible gambling activities adopted under the responsible gambling programme;
(j)details of the jurisdictions, casinos or responsible gambling bodies chosen by the casino operator for the purpose of comparing and improving the quality and standard of the responsible gambling measures adopted by the casino operator for the casino;
[S 652/2026 wef 21/09/2026]
(k)a statement by the person or committee appointed or to be appointed by the casino operator to supervise the responsible gambling programme for the casino, that the responsible gambling programme as and when implemented will satisfy the responsible gambling requirements applicable to the casino operator;
[S 652/2026 wef 21/09/2026]
(l)such other details as the Authority may require to determine whether the responsible gambling programme satisfies the responsible gambling requirements applicable to it.
[S 652/2026 wef 21/09/2026]
(3) The Authority shall not approve any responsible gambling programme submitted under this regulation unless the Authority is of the opinion that the responsible gambling programme satisfies or will satisfy all the responsible gambling requirements applicable to the casino operator.
[S 652/2026 wef 21/09/2026]
(4) The Authority may, by notice in writing served on the casino operator of a casino —
(a)approve a responsible gambling programme for the casino to which the application relates, subject to such conditions as the Authority thinks fit; or
[S 652/2026 wef 21/09/2026]
(b)reject the responsible gambling programme if any part of it does not satisfy any of the responsible gambling requirements applicable to the casino operator or does not comply with any of the requirements set out in these Regulations.
